# The status line on every screen (docs/click-everything.md, Part 1; the owner's click audit and
# his design of 2026-10-14): the status row is the header's last line, across the window under the
# tabs and the link's state, so above every screen's body and next to the maps. On its left what
# an action said, on whichever screen it was said - where it was once drawn only in front of the
# map's statistics, along the foot of FLIGHT DATA's and FLIGHT PLAN's map, and every other screen's
# buttons that answer with a status message looked dead; on its right, on those two screens, the
# map's statistics, moved up out of the map's foot. FLIGHT DATA's tuning graph is under its map,
# so the map is next to the row. `status.drawn` is what the line drew in the frame, not what was
# set; `status-bar below tab-fly` also fails when the line is not on screen at all.
#
# Needs no link: tools/gui-headless.sh status-bar
screen experimental
window 1600x1200
budget 20
env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml

expect screen experimental

# EXPERIMENTAL: a tool not ported says so.
click experimental-but_dem
expect status.drawn DEM: not ported yet (NOT_DONE_YET_MATRIX.md, the EXPERIMENTAL row)
expect status-bar below tab-fly

# LOGS > Review a log: Open with no name asks for one.
click tab-logs
click logs-tab-review
click log-open
expect status.drawn type the name of a log to open
expect status-bar below tab-fly

# CONFIG > Planner: the video's Start with no device chosen.
click tab-config
click config-page-ConfigPlanner
click planner-BUT_videostart
expect status.drawn Camera Fail: no Video Device and Video Format chosen
expect status-bar below tab-fly

# FLIGHT DATA, which drew it before under its map: Ctrl+T with no port chosen. The row is above the
# map, the map's statistics at its right, and the tuning graph's button under the map.
click tab-fly
key ctrl+t
expect status.drawn choose a port first
expect status-bar below tab-fly
expect status-row below tab-fly
expect map below status-row
expect map-status right-of status-bar
expect map-status below tab-fly
expect tuning-show below map

# FLIGHT PLAN: the same row above its map, the message kept from FLIGHT DATA.
click tab-plan
expect screen plan
expect status.drawn choose a port first
expect map below status-row
expect map-status right-of status-bar
